SCRIPT='A grievance essay: generational hook; 86% purchasing-power claim; housing price-to-income 1988 vs 2022, bubble and UK comparisons; homes vs CPI since 1990; demand factors (population, marriage, Pew living arrangements); student debt and tuition; credential inflation and starting salaries; car payments, gas and insurance; credit cards; latte objection; social media; gig economy; retirement (Social Security, pensions); healthcare; childcare and child cost; mental health; systemic-change argument; tech concentration; international comparison; practical tips (rent share, 3-5% down, avoid car payments); close. Directly verified (FRED): 1988 $110,000 and 2022 $433,000 median home prices; stated incomes wrong ($27,230 and $74,580), so the 1988 ratio is right but 2022 is 5.8, not over 6. CPI multiplier is 2.48x, not 2.31x. Unsupported: 86% purchasing-power loss; healthcare tripled. The stored ending is complete; heavy filler words.'
